@startuml
title Multithreaded Data Acquisition Pipeline - Write Side Component Diagram

left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle uml2

component "Pipeline CLI\n<<external driver>>" as CLI

component "Write Side Subsystem" as WriteSide {
  portin commandPort
  portin bufferPort
  portout sinkPort

  component "ioPipelineController" as Controller
  component "ioUsbWriteController\n<<consumer>>" as WriteWorker
  queue "ioDataBuffer\n<<shared buffer>>" as Buffer
  component "ioFileByteStream" as FileSink
  component "ioFtdiOutputByteStream" as FtdiSink

  () "pipelineLifecycle" as PipelineLifecycle
  () "writerControl" as WriterControl
  () "bufferReader" as BufferReader
  () "ioWritableByteStream" as WritableContract
}

PipelineLifecycle - Controller
WriterControl - WriteWorker
BufferReader - Buffer
WritableContract - FileSink
WritableContract - FtdiSink

CLI ..> commandPort : pipeline command
commandPort --> Controller : delegation
bufferPort --> WriteWorker : buffered bytes
WriteWorker --> sinkPort : delegated output

Controller ..> WriterControl : configure + start
Controller ..> WritableContract : select output mode
WriteWorker ..> BufferReader : pop()
WriteWorker ..> WritableContract : write_bytes()

note bottom of WriteSide
The write side consumes bytes from the shared buffer
through one contract and forwards them to the selected
output adapter through ioWritableByteStream.
end note
@enduml
